  "metadata": {
    "name": "nr-industrial-county",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.5 step 7e: the `nr-industrial-county` RunSpec computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE -- Cook County, Illinois, August 2020, weekday, sector 3 (Industrial), onroad diesel, CO, NOx and PM10. NONROAD'S WHOLE INVENTORY: the diesel selection matches no nonroad fuel ID, so every SCC runs -- gasoline, diesel, LPG, CNG and marine, 1,084 equipment points, 5,267 cohorts, 15,801 rows, all reproduced at 7.207e-06.\n\nIt found four of the five rules: the per-technology sulfur alternates and the diesel PM correction, the renormalized technology sets, the per-technology clamp, and the nearest rate bin (`2270003030` has a point at exactly 11 hp). A narrowed probe -- one sector's diesel, `runspecfueltype` 23 -- reproduced the cells it covers in three minutes where the run takes nine."
  },
